gomodel:6ab067da00014326
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "STC2 inhibits PAPPA by forming a covalent 2:2 complex (STC2 Cys120 disulfide) that blocks IGFBP4 binding at an exosite; the active site stays accessible (PMID:25533459, 36257932, 36550107; full texts). Modelled as metalloendopeptidase inhibitor activity although the inhibition is covalent (disulfide), not catalytic modification. STC2 also inhibits PAPPA2 (PMID:26195635); PAPPA2 arm effect on IGF1R signaling inferred (IC). IGF1R assay: 293-IGF1R cells, PMID:25533459. IGFBP5 sequestering is IC (PMID:10766744, abstract only). Not modelled: UPR/PERK-ATF4 induction of STC2 (PMID:15485913). Built by claude4go from Swiss-Prot PAM_STC1.log." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. STC2 covalent inhibition of PAPPA blocks IGFBP4 proteolysis and IGF1 release, negatively regulating IGF1R signaling (Human)." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "production" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052" ;
        dc:date                "2026-11-24" ;
        dc:title               "Negative regulation of IGF1R signaling by STC2 (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "https://www.uniprot.org" , "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00014326 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

